  "experiment": {
    "hypothesis": "The explicit completion BEGIN, advisory lock, identity SELECT, DELETE, and COMMIT add avoidable PostgreSQL round trips; one identity-bound autocommit DELETE should preserve INDEXED recovery semantics while reducing final reply latency.",
    "implementation": "The completion DELETE constrained all sixteen durable intent identity fields and INDEXED state in one PostgreSQL statement. Timeout or connection errors still reconciled under the existing advisory-lock load_intent path; an absent row remained idempotent success.",
